# Keep secrets, backups, VCS metadata, and heavy build artifacts OUT of the
# Docker build context. Critically: never bake .env (DB/Garage/LLM secrets) into
# the image — runtime config is injected by compose `env_file`, not the image.
# (Also: a root-owned .env.bak from an ops change was breaking `docker build`
# because the unprivileged build user couldn't read it; excluding it fixes that.)

# Secrets + their backups (any .env variant)
.env
.env.*
*.env

# Stray backup files from ops changes
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak.*

# VCS
.git
.gitignore

# Python caches / build
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# JS/Next build artifacts (the app image is the Python backend; it never needs
# these, and they bloat the context massively)
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Misc
*.log
.DS_Store
